## ⏱️ 7. Regulatory Notification Clocks

The clocks start on *awareness*, not on root cause. Several will expire before your investigation concludes — which is why every regime below permits an initial partial report, and why "we'll notify once we understand it" is the most common compliance failure in AI incidents.

| Regime | Trigger | Clock | Notes |
|--------|---------|-------|-------|
| **EU AI Act Art. 73** | Serious incident involving a high-risk AI system | **15 days** general · **10 days** if a death may have been caused · **2 days** for widespread infringement or serious/irreversible disruption of critical infrastructure | Art. 73(5) expressly allows an **initial incomplete report** with supplementary detail to follow. Commission draft guidance issued Oct 2025 |
| **GDPR Art. 33** | Personal data breach | **72 hours** to the supervisory authority | Art. 34 adds notification to data subjects where high risk to rights and freedoms |
| **NIS2** | Significant incident, in-scope entities | **24h** early warning · **72h** assessment · **1 month** final | Runs in parallel with, not instead of, the above |
| **Sectoral** (DORA, HIPAA, SEC, state laws) | Varies | Varies | Map yours in advance — per-incident research is not a plan |

**Timing caveat as of September 2026:** Art. 73 sits within the high-risk regime, and the **Digital Omnibus** (Council approval 29 June 2026) moved stand-alone Annex III high-risk obligations to **2 December 2027** (Annex I product-embedded to 2 August 2028), on standards-readiness rather than substantive grounds. Sources published before mid-2026 still cite August 2026 — check the vintage of anything you're relying on. **Confirm applicability, trigger definitions, and dates with counsel for your specific systems and markets; this is not legal advice.**

**Operational implication:** build the notification decision into the runbook at the 15-minute mark (see RB-4 step 3), not at the retrospective. Pre-draft the partial-report template with the fields each regime requires, and pre-agree who signs it.

